item(2,[2,54],'self-flagged step',[97,134,136],['4-45','1535-1554','1624-1631'],'g(x)(y)=-\\psi(y)x; mais c’est aussi OK.','For 0→L→E→O→0, the alternating pairing g(x)(y)=ψ(x)y−ψ(y)x induces −id on L and id on the quotient. With L invertible its determinant-twisted dual is canonically identified with E.','Local exactness and invertibility explain the isomorphism; the doubtful symbol in the subsequent Q/N correspondence remains unresolved.','agrees','Both endpoint evaluations are explicit on97, and134/136 repeat the same formula. The note correctly limits what the completed sign check proves.')
item(3,[3],'unproved claim',[98],['64-76'],'Q_N(\\varphi_N(x))=-N(x)\\delta_N','The author asserts this discriminant identity for any rank-two locally free module carrying a quadratic form, without supplementary algebra structure.','Definitions must be recovered from earlier sheets; the sign-sensitive coordinate interpretation is a reconstruction, not supplied fully on98. Root companion checks earlier47/53 and distinguishes their opposite sign.','agrees','The inserted rank2 and “sans autre donnée” are present. The minus in local N is explicitly doubtful and is not repaired.')
item(4,[4],'withdrawn in the same text',[99,100,102],['91-120','146-154','192-211'],'\\alpha\\circ\\mathrm{inc}=2\\beta; Je pense à l’hom','A proposed construction of a transpose by boundary maps is crossed out; the operator 1+σ1⊗σ2 returns in the live construction.','The cancellation concerns this derivation, not the later trace operator as a whole.','agrees','The whole block91–120 is deleted, whereas100 and102 carry the surviving construction.')
item(5,[5],'unproved claim',[100],['124-154'],'un sens sans utiliser les structures de rev.','Under the duality identifications for line-module extensions, the transpose of E1⊗E2→E defines A→A1⊗A2 before imposing quadratic forms or χ=2.','A linear transpose is well defined when the pairings are perfect; it is not thereby an algebra homomorphism or a coherent monoidal comparison.','agrees','The page expressly separates the transpose from the specialization to quadratic covers.')
item(6,[6],'unpursued implication',[101,102],['159-188','192-211'],'Trace réduite; soient égaux','The rank-two product module is the pushout of the tensor boundary A1⊔O A2 along the common reduced trace. A map out of this pushout requires agreement of the scalar and tensor maps on the boundary.','The universal-property formulation spells out the diagram; multiplication and global coherence require further arguments.','agrees','The compatibility is written at101 and checked on factor elements at102.')
item(7,[7,9],'unproved claim',[102,104,105],['213-226','276-278','336-348'],'est univ injectif, et a pour image; on ne sait pas si','For quadratic algebras A1,A2, if at every characteristic2 point at least one is étale, the product A maps universally injectively to B=A1⊗A2 with image B^(σ1⊗σ2). Without that hypothesis injectivity and surjectivity may fail.','The cover D(2)∪D(b1)∪D(b2) and invariant-equation proof are editorial and verified independently in this run.','agrees','The later general doubt does not retract the conditional NB. Abstract A and its image are kept distinct.')
item(8,[8,12],'unproved claim',[103,105,106],['245-271','355-359','362-388'],'une application quadratique unique','For quadratic A1,A2 over R there is a unique R-quadratic N:B=A1⊗A2→A1∧A2 whose pure-tensor values are N1(x1)N2(x2) and whose polarization is Tr_B/A(x·bar y). It satisfies iN(x)=x·bar x.','The pages propose then assert existence/uniqueness; our complete integral coefficient verification appears separately as SA02-13. The four values alone would not determine a quadratic map in characteristic2.','agrees','The two conditions, not the image equation alone, are the proposition’s characterization.')
item(10,[10],'reading question',[104],['279-305'],'b=b_1b_2; c=b_1^2c_2+b_2^2c_1-4c_1c_2','With ui²+biui+ci=0, the product generator t satisfies t²+b1b2t+C=0, C=b1²c2+b2²c1−4c1c2, and maps to2u1u2+b1u2+b2u1. Its discriminant is the product of the input discriminants.','The discriminant multiplication is an algebraic deduction. A modern paper’s opposite generator convention must be translated explicitly.','agrees','All coefficients and the generator image occur exactly as the note says; independent universal reduction is zero.')
item(11,[11],'unpursued implication',[103,105],['233-243','331-348'],'i(Tr(ξ))=ξ+bar ξ; Tr(i(η))=2η','The trace B→A takes basis(1,u1,u2,u1u2) to(2,−b1,−b2,t+b1b2), is A-linear, and factors 1+σ1⊗σ2; its reverse composite is2id.','A-linearity and the nonprojector warning are verified by integral coefficients; no cancellation of2 is used.','agrees','The manuscript gives both composites. Division by2 would add a hypothesis.')
item(13,[13],'idea of the earlier run',[103,105,106,107],['245-271','355-427'],'les éléments de la base 1,U_1,U_2,U_1⊗U_2','Earlier-run reconstruction: for x=x0+x1u+x2v+x3uv, N(x)=x0²+c1x1²+c2x2²+c1c2x3²−b1x0x1−b2x0x2+(t+b1b2)x0x3−tx1x2−b2c1x1x3−b1c2x2x3. This is multiplicative and A-quadratic with the required trace polarization.','The polynomial is not fully written by Grothendieck here. It is an earlier-run completion, independently checked over Z[b1,b2,c1,c2] in this run, including regular-representation determinants.','agrees','The note correctly distinguishes its coefficient completion from the pages. The fresh 18-identity certificate confirms the claimed algebraic identities, not historical priority.')
item(14,[14],'self-flagged step',[106,107],['375-427'],'Prouvons p.ex. la première; N\\bar N=N_{A/O}(N) OK','N_A/R∘N_B/A=N_B/R and Tr_A/R∘Tr_B/A=Tr_B/R for the genuine quadratic inputs. Partial conjugations act by the canonical involution of A and total conjugation preserves N.','The source suppresses i in a product equality; the scalar conclusion is justified since R→B is faithful. Our determinant/trace calculation supplies a direct proof.','agrees','Norm transitivity ends OK; trace transitivity and conjugation identities are stated. The omitted map is not cancelled without justification.')
item(15,[15],'unpursued implication',[107,108,110],['431-447','454-459','574-607'],'ni même plat; soit injective','Quasi-quadratic data permit a nonflat algebra and a noninjective scalar map α:k→A. Their axioms force ker α to have2λ=0 and λ²=0 for each λ in the kernel.','The kernel consequence follows from t(λ1)=2λ and n(λ1)=λ²; it is an earlier-run deduction, not an extra manuscript axiom.','agrees','Nonflatness and nonfaithfulness are explicitly allowed; replacing this object by a rank-two locally free algebra would be incorrect.')
item(16,[16],'withdrawn in the same text',[108],['498-519'],'donc on a bien n(\\bar x)=n(x)','The separate axiom label for n(bar x)=n(x) is deleted, but the assertion is immediately proved by n(t(x)1−x)=n(x)+t(x)²−t(x)².','Only quadraticity, the trace polarization at1, and n(1)=1 are needed; multiplicativity and injectivity are unnecessary.','agrees','It is the redundancy of an axiom, not the conclusion, that is withdrawn.')
item(17,[17],'unpursued implication',[108,109],['483-496','529-553'],'Au facteur 2 près','For the stated quasi-quadratic data, 2xy=t(x)y+t(y)x−α(φ_n(x,y)). Thus if2 is invertible the pointed module and quadratic form determine multiplication and α is injective.','The second formula is obtained by substituting φ_n(x,y)=t(x bar y). No reconstruction of two-torsion multiplication is asserted.','agrees','The author’s factor2 warning is mathematically exact; a division-free identity is retained.')
item(18,[18],'unpursued implication',[109],['523-553'],'sans supposer α injectif','The norm identity yields α(φ_n(y,z))=α(t(y bar z)); equality in k is automatic only when α is injective and is otherwise a separate requirement.','This is a distinction between target values and their images, not a new theorem about ordinary quadratic algebras.','agrees','The source first derives the faithful case and then explicitly imposes the general case.')
item(19,[19],'reading question',[109,110],['555-563','600-607'],'Une formule facultative; identité de (2n)-formes','If k/k0 has finite locally free rank n and A/k0 rank2n, trace/norm tower compatibility is optional additional data. The norm identity is an equality of degree2n polynomial forms.','The manuscript’s five-axiom definition excludes the optional sixth item; pointwise finite-field checking is not equivalent to checking a polynomial law.','agrees','The ranks and facultative status are explicit on both sheets.')
item(20,[20],'reading question',[108,110],['454-496','574-607'],'n(xy)=n(x)n(y); satisfaisant 1° à 5°','The first list requires n multiplicative; the five-axiom recap omits this requirement. The omission is not logically redundant for the expressly allowed nonfaithful scalar maps.','Whether this was an intended weaker definition or an abbreviated recap cannot be decided from the text. SA02-21 is the explicit separation.','agrees','Read lists differ exactly in this clause; no unmarked emendation is made.')
item(21,[21],'idea of the earlier run',[108,110],['454-496','574-607'],'algèbre quasi-quadratique','Counterexample to equivalence of the two lists: k=Z/4, A=F2[e,f]/(e²,f²), t(a+be+cf+def)=2a, n=a+2d. All five recap axioms hold; n(ef)=2 while n(e)n(f)=0, and failure also occurs on units.','Over every Z/4-algebra S the law is a²+2d² on(S/2S)^4 using arbitrary lifts. This lift-independent formula proves the base-change assertion beyond a finite point test.','agrees','Independent exhaustive check confirms zero axiom failures and96 multiplicativity failures among256 pairs; polynomial-law extension is justified separately.')
item(22,[22],'other',[111],['612-642'],'sans forcément supposer ... injectif','Data: three quasi-quadratic k-algebras Ai, maps Ai→A, and quasi-quadratic structures A/Ai. Neither faithful maps, generation, nor any finite locally free rank is initially assumed.','This is the exact object class for subsequent compatibilities, not automatically a biquadratic field extension.','agrees','The four data groups and both noninjectivity qualifications are present.')
item(23,[23],'withdrawn in the same text',[111,114],['643-654','724-741'],'On veut la condition σ1σ2σ3=1','For involutions σi, the relation σ1σ2σ3=1 entails pairwise commutation and σiσj=σk. It is deleted at111 and imposed afresh as condition3 at114.','Validity on the subalgebra generated by Ai extends to A only with generation.','agrees','The later live axiom prevents treating the earlier cancellation as rejection of the relation.')
item(24,[24],'unpursued implication',[112],['658-685'],'un des 6 diagrammes; s’annule au moins sur le noyau','For each ordered i≠j, require Tjαi=ti and Njαi=ni, interpreting scalars in Aj. Trace compatibility is factorization of ti⊗id through Ai⊗Aj→A, not an assertion this map is injective or surjective.','The six cases mean3×2 ordered pairs; the full list is reconstructed from the representative diagram.','agrees','The margin explicitly denies quadraticity and generation; hence the compatibility remains imposed data.')
item(25,[25],'self-flagged step',[113,114],['690-722'],'Il reste à vérifier; O.K.','Under the preceding trace, involution and norm compatibilities, the induced norm diagram agrees on pure tensors and polar forms, hence as quadratic laws. Conversely norm compatibility implies trace compatibility by comparing a and1+a.','The literal t1/n1 and A1/A2 mistakes are isolated in SA02-26; the well-typed proof uses n1 and base change to A2.','agrees','The polar-form verification is explicitly completed; it should not remain an unresolved author doubt.')
item(26,[26],'reading question',[113],['696-704'],'t_1(x_1)·x_2²; par chgt. de base k→A_1','Two frozen tokens fail the displayed types: the pure-tensor norm value should involve n1(x1), and the base-change target in this diagram is A2.','Suggested n1 and A2 are mathematical alternatives for a future ink inspection, not corrections adopted here.','agrees','The surrounding norm diagram and the preceding margin supply the type checks. Both readings enter Stage4.')
item(27,[27],'self-flagged step',[114],['743-765'],'du moins si k−A injectif; on la suppose ... en tous cas','The involution relation and trace restrictions give equal images of tiTi in A; equality in k follows if k→A is injective and is otherwise separately assumed. With common T, 2x=T1x+T2x+T3x−T(x).','The common trace assumption must be retained in any general theorem with nonfaithful scalars.','agrees','The margin supplies the missing scalar-level hypothesis expressly.')
item(28,[28],'self-flagged step',[115],['770-816'],'si k−A est injectif; O.K.','When k→A is injective, the four-conjugate computation proves n1N1=n2N2=n3N3 and N1(x)N2(x)N3(x)=x²N_A/k(x), interpreting all products in A.','Without injectivity it proves equality of images only. The xi are conjugatesσi(x), as the permutation table requires.','agrees','The provisional expectation is crossed out and replaced by this qualified proof; the Ti/σi token remains a scan issue.')
item(29,[29],'unpursued implication',[116,117],['820-859'],'Il n’y a pas en général d’opération de ce groupe sur A','The tensor product carries F2³, while the compatible action on A is Γ=ker(sum:F2³→F2), with nonzero elements011,101,110 acting via relative involutions. Faithfulness is not asserted.','The algebra-generation argument explains why independent flips need not descend.','agrees','The source explicitly contrasts the full group with the even subgroup, and crosses out001.')
item(30,[30,31],'unproved claim',[117],['863-877'],'deux au moins des A_i soient non étales','For actual quadratic Ai, the triple product B0→(A1⊗A2⊗A3)^Γ is an isomorphism away from characteristic2 points where at least two inputs are nonétale.','Earlier-run proof: after inverting2 use vi=2ui+bi and invariant basis1,v1v2v3; when two inputs are étale split them faithfully flat and use the transitive four-factor action. We recheck both arguments. This is sufficient, not a necessity theorem.','agrees','The excluded locus in the sentence is exact; the explicit proof in entry31 is editorial and merged with the same assertion.')
item(32,[32],'conjecture',[118],['884-903'],'j’ai envie de ... prouver; à valeurs dans k.1_A','With the enlarged three-algebra compatibilities and injective k→A, the author seeks scalar image of the map B0=A1∧A2∧A3→A, equivalently factorization of Spec A through a section of the triple cover.','A^Γ=k is sufficient and is stronger than scalar image of this particular map. The programme is not disproved solely by excess invariants.','agrees','The source introduces a goal, then a sufficient condition and a characteristic2 warning.')
item(33,[33],'idea of the earlier run',[118],['895-903'],'pas tjrs vérifiée ... à cause de la car.2','Over F2 take A=F2[e,f]/(e²,f²), Ai generated by e,f,e+f. Each pair tensor map is an isomorphism; relative conjugations are identity, so A^Γ=A≠F2. The triple product is F2[t]/t² and t maps to0, so scalar image still holds.','This explicit degeneration is the earlier run’s example, independently verified by bases and squaring.','agrees','It realizes, rather than refutes, the source’s distinction between scalar-image goal and sufficient invariant-ring condition.')
item(34,[34],'self-flagged step',[118,119],['899-921'],'a=1/4 T_{A/k}(a)∈k O.K.','Under the common-trace compatibility, every invariant a obeys4a=T_A/k(a). If2 is invertible then A^Γ=k·1.','This is the four-element subgroup calculation; no averaging over all eight tensor symmetries is used.','agrees','The factor4 and the hypothesis that2 is invertible are explicit and the arithmetic is correct.')
item(35,[35],'unproved claim',[119,120,121],['925-964'],'enfin A^Γ=k.1_A; par twist','If all Ai are quadratic étale, k→A is injective, the Ai generate A, and A^Γ=k, then Spec A is the parity fibre of a section of the triple product and each pair projection is an isomorphism; conversely every such twisted parity fibre has these properties.','The proof is repaired only at the standalone lemma’s target and closedness; closedness is already supplied by generation in the actual proposition.','agrees','The insertion of the invariant-ring condition is essential; it cannot be dropped from the proposition.')
item(36,[36,37],'reading question',[120,121],['948-964'],'k→Γ(X_J,O_{X_J}); un sous-schéma','The frozen lemma is false: its ambient-target injectivity is automatic for nonempty J. Even changing the target to Γ(Xcal,O) is insufficient unless Xcal is closed. Corrected theorem: a Γ-stable closed subscheme of disjoint copies X_J with transitive Γ-action and faithful scalar ring map is all X_J.','Two explicit counterexamples: J={*}, k=Z, Xcal=Spec F2 for the literal target; Xcal=D(2) for the target-corrected but nonclosed formulation. The intended ideal proof works with the corrected target and closedness.','agrees','Both flaws are visible mathematically and both counterexamples check every written hypothesis; neither emends the transcription. The closedness diagnosis from entry37 is merged into the same lemma.')
item(38,[38,41],'conjecture',[121,122],['967-1014'],'J’ai envie de vérifier ... sans condition étale; Tr1 doit être B0-linéaire','Given three arbitrary finite locally free quadratic covers and a section of their contracted triple product, endow the inverse image with compatible quasi-biquadratic structures over the three inputs. The universal construction requests relative traces/norms B→Ai⊗B0.','The manuscript only begins B0-linearity/quadraticity requirements; a full quasi-quadratic structure requires the relevant Ai⊗B0 module compatibilities and five axioms. No finite locally free rank4 claim is built into this problem.','agrees','The task is expressly prospective at121 and still unfinished at122; the final norm label and ellipsis supply no completed construction.')
item(39,[39,40],'self-flagged step',[122],['984-1014'],'n’est pas même fini loc. libre, ni même plat','The universal morphism from the full triple cover to its contracted triple product is finite and surjective, but may be nonflat. Over F2 with three dual-number inputs, B0=F2[t]/t² maps to B=F2[e,f,g]/(e²,f²,g²) by t↦0; the unique fibre has dimension8.','Earlier-run example independently verified. Tensoring (t)↪B0 with B gives the zero map from a nonzero module, proving nonflatness. Surjectivity is separate from injectivity of the algebra map.','agrees','The exclamation-marked4 and2 labels cannot be turned into proved relative ranks. Entry40 supplies the same phenomenon with a worked example.')

item(42,[42,43],'self-flagged step',[124],['1018-1028'],'απ=π′β ⇔ βω=ω′γ ?','For a morphism of short exact rows, compatibility with χ-retractions is equivalent to compatibility with their complementary χ-sections when aπ+ωq=χid and a′π′+ω′q′=χid.','This is a conditional answer from the earlier run. Subtract the two complementary identities and cancel only the monomorphism a′ or the epimorphism q, never χ. The source itself stops at a question.','agrees','The two question marks and unfinished calculation are real. Entry43 supplies the exact hypotheses and proof of the same question, not an unconditional reading.')
