def narrative(n,scan,lines,words,statement,qualification,kind='other'):
 item(n,[n],kind,[scan],lines,words,statement,'Archival testimony only; no independent psychological, medical, or biographical validation is claimed.','agrees',qualification)
narrative(76,125,['1052-1061'],'dénouement probable','The reused essay forecasts a possible planetary catastrophe as the culmination of competition for force and power.','The predictive/probable wording is recorded; no quantitative likelihood is supplied.')
narrative(77,125,['1063-1077'],'inséparables et complémentaires par nature','He introduces yin/yang and woman/man as names for complementary aspects in his own interpretive model.','This is his vocabulary and conceptual assertion, not an established universal psychological classification.')
narrative(78,125,['1079-1088'],'Il semblerait','He proposes that childhood affirmation/rejection mechanisms largely govern later behaviour.','The modal qualification is explicit; later qualifications must not be dropped.')
narrative(79,127,['1131-1144'],'raisons qui restent encore mystérieuses','He divides his inward history into three periods, beginning the last inJuly1976, and leaves the cause of his trajectory mysterious.','This is an autobiographical explanatory gap, not an unfinished algebraic proof.')
narrative(80,127,['1146-1163'],'un mystère','He interprets his parents’ values and asks how he flourished in the environment he describes.','His attribution of others’ inward states remains testimony; the admitted puzzle coexists with it.')
narrative(81,129,['1221-1232'],'ne tarderait pas à les prouver','He recalls expecting Deligne to prove the Weil and standard conjectures around his1970departure; the statement also contains his characterization ofDeligne.','The note reports a recollection; the actual Weil proof and its date are separate literature facts. Opening double-negative syntax remains a reading issue.')
narrative(82,129,['1234-1246'],'dont je ne suis pas plus convaincu que lui','He expresses doubt about the standard conjectures while insisting that the importance of the question does not depend on their truth.','This is a position on an open mathematical question, not a proof or a present-day status report.')
narrative(83,129,['1246-1252'],'deux questions les plus fondamentales','He pairs standard conjectures on cycles with resolution of singularities as two fundamental research questions and anticipates their fertility.','The actual mathematical problems are indexed separately; the priority ranking is his assessment.')
narrative(84,131,['1318-1354'],'approbation automatique','He distinguishes childhood identification with his father from automatic approval and describes disagreement at violence toward his sister.','Both admiration and its explicit limitation are retained as his testimony.')
narrative(85,133,['1465-1480'],'se placerait dans ma huitième année','He tentatively locates an inward rupture around his eighth year, within a few months.','An exact calendar date is not computed from these qualified recollections.')
narrative(86,133,['1482-1495'],'Peut-être le mystère n’est plus','He tentatively relocates the puzzle from absence of inner conflict to his parents’ capacity to accept him.','This revises the explanation sought, without retracting the described childhood experience.')
narrative(87,135,['1583-1599'],'rectifier le tir','He distinguishes acceptance of a child from indulgence or automatic approval of every act.','The source gives examples and vocabulary, not a general proven developmental theory.')
narrative(88,135,['1605-1620'],'peut-être toujours; J’ai tendance à croire','He conjectures a lasting dominantyin/yangnote while admitting inability to identify his own.','Both modal limits and the unresolved personal case are explicit.')
narrative(89,137,['1681-1698'],'Ce n’est pas le lieu ... tous ces signes','He tentatively describes his creative force as predominantly feminine and defers reviewing supporting signs.','The note does not fill the stated evidentiary gap or infer an identity beyond his words.')
narrative(90,137,['1700-1721'],'c’est surtout je crois','He attributes lack of remembered humiliation to secure acceptance and speculates that boys’ doll play is discouraged.','These are qualified recollections/causal interpretations, not comparative research findings.')
narrative(91,139,['1789-1815'],'quarante-six ans plus tard','A5October note recallsDecember1933and dates the later investigation toAugust1979–October1980.','Event, investigation, and note date are distinct; none dates the mathematics.',kind='title, date or page count')
narrative(92,141,['1928-1934'],'Il a fallu','The unfinished sentence on printed473continues with pourtant plusieurs années on printed474 at scan145 despite intervening scan143/page480.','This is a textual join in printed-page order, not authorization to reorder the diplomatic transcription.',kind='reading question')
